Original commit body from ed59229b913999316e26688b15c41a88f70fec5d:

#1953 turned a module_attr_ref read of an in-tree module object's member
into a references edge, but gated it per MODULE: a module the file also
bound by name or default was left alone, because the attribute emitter
keys its edges by module, not by the alias the read went through. The
filed INV-nuzas fixture is exactly that shape -- `const { helper } =
require('@ws/b'); const b = require('@ws/b'); new b.Engine()` -- so its
javascript:@ws/b:0-0:@ws/b.Engine stand-in survived the fix (found
re-running the filed repro on merged dev).

_module_object_reads now walks the file's member_expression nodes and
records (line, module, attribute) for each read made THROUGH a
module-object alias (import * as, a plain require), and separately for
reads through a named or default binding. An edge is retargeted only if
its (line, module, attribute) is a module-object read that no other
binding also produces. `W.Builder` after `import { W } from './w'` (a
property of the exported object) is still left alone.

Measured, analyze_javascript edge set, branch vs origin/dev js_ts.py: knex
1 (lib/schema/tablecompiler.js:306 `helpers.normalizeArr`, which binds
../util/helpers both as `helpers` and by destructuring -- the case #1953
missed), blocksuite 5 (note-edgeless-block.ts, `import { X } from
'./note-edgeless-block.css'` beside `import * as styles from` the same),
each read against its source line; nuclear's named-object reads unchanged;
apollo-server, jotai, hls.js, pm2, ioredis 0. Line pins into js_ts.py
relocated by anchor (module_key_axis 7819 -> 7835, 1354 -> 1370;
signature_axis 6559 -> 6575).

Test: the filed shape (a module bound by destructuring and as a module
object) through run_behavior_map. Four mutations (other-alias reads
ignored, every alias a module object, no per-read gate, no module-object
reads) each turn a test red.

Addresses WI-halol and INV-nuzas.

